<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22632" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incŭbo</span></b> , ōnis,
			m.
		1. incubo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who lies upon</i> any thing. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A spirit that watches over buried treasures</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum modo incuboni pileum rapuisset, thesaurum
					invenit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. Fragm. Trag. 38, 8</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The nightmare</i>, <i>incubus</i>
			(post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ab incubone deludi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 100</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de incubone praesumptio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 44</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
